Subject: Tests for crafting by confirmed window clicks, with Paper's result burst

Applies to: https://github.com/aibengineering/mine-ai-mcp at 2fe1306a0ac51efa99154048e65f2caff00a8934 plus
0001-craft-by-confirmed-window-clicks.patch (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 AI Bengineering; see
../../LICENSE-mine-ai-mcp.txt). Kept by Picasso Lab (UC San Diego) for "Muse plays Minecraft".

src/test-support/click-server.ts is a bot double with a server's side of windows (ported from the agent's
test/fake-bot.js): it applies each window_click to its own copy of the window with vanilla's click rules and the
version's recipes, answers with a resync after a lag, and with `paper: true` also sends Paper's burst around a
crafting result (the result slot empty, then filled, then one more resync). src/world/confirmed-craft.test.ts runs
executeCraftPlan against it: the 2x2 grid and a table under Paper's bursts with exact server counts, batches that use
the room a batch frees, the inventory-room refusal before any click, a silent server, a table that never opens, and
cancellation half way (the grid is still handed back). Run with `bun test src/world/confirmed-craft.test.ts`.

